  "extraction_notes": "MNIST is the only dataset with full hardware mapping and energy/area numbers (partly measured on 96-device Y-Flash arrays, partly simulated). Table 5 accuracies (Iris, CIFAR2, KWS6, F-MNIST, EMG, Gesture Phase, Human Activity) are given without split, T/s, or energy, and it is unclear whether they are software or hardware-mapped accuracies; split marked 'test' by assumption. Table 6 baselines on other datasets (DNN/PCM [27] CIFAR-10 93.7%/11.9 TOPS/W, CNN/ReRAM [28] CIFAR-10 91.9%/51.4 TOPS/W, CNN/STT-MRAM [30] CIFAR-100 21.4 TOPS/W, CNN/ReRAM [31] CIFAR-10 92.1%/27.2 TOPS/W) were omitted as results because they are not on datasets this paper evaluates. Device-level metrics (programming 139 nJ avg, erasing 0.8 pJ, read LCS 3.2e-5 pJ, read HCS 0.05 pJ) are in Table 4 and not repeated as results."
